feat(worklog): multi-day shifts — record an explicit end date end-to-end

A WorkLog now stores an explicit EndDate alongside EndTime, so a shift can
legitimately span more than 24 hours (e.g. an admin closing a long
forgotten clock-out, or an overnight made explicit). Previously a shift
was capped at a single overnight (≤24h) because only an end-of-day HH:mm
was stored and overnight was inferred.

Domain + persistence:
- WorkLog gains nullable EndDate; End()/CreateManual()/Update() take it,
  with derive-overnight overloads so callers that only have an end time
  keep the historical ≤24h behaviour.
- Migration AddWorkLogEndDate adds the column and backfills closed rows
  (EndDate = WorkDate, or WorkDate+1 when EndTime <= StartTime). MUST be
  deployed in a maintenance window with a DB backup.

Hours are date-aware everywhere:
- ShiftHours.CalcHours(startDate,startTime,endDate,endTime) computes a true
  datetime span; DeriveEndDate() infers the overnight date for time-only
  flows. Updated all read sites: GetMyWorkLogs, GetAllWorkLogs, GetReport,
  GetPayrollExport (the dashboard "tonight" totals stay a same-night
  estimate). WorkLogDto / ShiftDetailRow / ActiveStaffDto now carry EndDate.

Commands:
- EndWorkLog (staff clock-out) + CreateManual + the staff edit form derive
  EndDate (overnight, ≤24h) — no UI change.
- AdminEndShift (dashboard Close shift) + UpdateWorkLog (Reports Edit shift)
  take an explicit end date and allow >24h, capped at 14 days as a typo
  guard; overlap detection is now date-explicit.

Frontend:
- shared-lib models + WorkLogService.update/adminEndShift carry endDate.
- Reports Edit-shift dialog gains an End Date picker (defaults to start
  date); dashboard Close-shift already sends it. i18n en+zh.

Tests: AdminEndShift now covers multi-day accepted + >14-day rejected +
overnight; entity overloads keep existing suites intact. Backend
Application 386, shared-lib 310, admin 454, staff 216 — all green.
Verified live (Docker): migration backfilled 3/3 closed shifts; an edit
to a >24h span was accepted (24.4h, EndDate next day) and reverted cleanly.

